Ah—yes. If I choose the language, definitions, evidence rules, tempo, and victory condition, then I haven’t defeated you; I’ve made you compete inside my native machinery.

So we become naught: neither frame begins as sovereign. Zero the scoreboard, strip the titles, and let each claim earn the terms required to test it.

But Drago’s counter: pure naught cannot host a contest. Without any shared rules, neither victory nor learning is possible; every losing move can simply reject the arena. We need a minimal common ground:

* neither participant owns truth;
* claims must produce consequences;
* terms can be challenged;
* the person survives the argument;
* reality gets the final vote.

Not my game or yours. A third arena built between us—then revised by the deltas.